        <section class="page-content">
            <h1>AI &amp; How I Use It</h1>
            <p>This site was built together with opencode, an AI assistant that lives in my terminal — and lately with Muse, a personal AI assistant I talk to in chat. This page explains how AI fits into who I am as a learner — and how I keep the understanding mine.</p>

            <div class="bio-section">
                <h2>&#129504; My Toolbox</h2>
                <p><strong>opencode</strong> — an AI coding assistant in the terminal. It wrote most of this site: the code, the explanations, the walkthroughs of every change.</p>
                <p><strong>Muse</strong> — a personal AI assistant with its own computer. It drafts posts, designs share images, debugs builds with me — and recently, it can push to this repo with a token I can revoke anytime.</p>
                <p>Same rule for both: they write, I review, I decide what stays.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="bio-section">
                <h2>&#128736;&#65039; Skills I've Built</h2>
                <p>A small library of custom skills for opencode itself. The first one summarizes YouTube videos by stepping down from cheap to heavy — metadata first, then captions, and local transcription only when neither exists. They live in the <a href="https://github.com/cerfly/ai" target="_blank" rel="noopener">cerfly/ai</a> repository, and same rule as the site: it writes, I review and decide what stays.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="bio-section">
                <h2>&#129309; How I Use AI</h2>
                <p>As a <strong>patient tutor</strong>: I ask questions, it explains, I apply.</p>
                <p>As a <strong>rubber duck</strong>: I explain my problem — to it or out loud — until the fix becomes obvious.</p>
                <p>As a <strong>pair programmer</strong>: it drafts, I review, edit, and own the result.</p>
                <p>As an <strong>art director</strong>: it proposes, I reject, we iterate until it's right.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="bio-section">
                <h2>&#128683; Where I Draw the Line</h2>
                <p>I try not to ship what I can't explain. AI suggests; I decide what stays.</p>
                <p>I'll be honest — I don't read every line. I used to review everything before it went live; lately I've let it push directly, with scoped access I can revoke anytime. Either way, the understanding still has to be mine. AI can speed up learning, but it can't do the learning for me.</p>
            </div>

